# Line-ending policy. core.autocrlf=true on Windows checkouts was rewriting shell
# scripts to CRLF, and the bot containers bind-mount ./scripts — a CRLF
# bot-entrypoint.sh makes the container shell die with `$'\r': command not found`.
# 2026-07-24: force LF on ALL text — a full re-checkout rewrote unpinned .js to CRLF
# on disk, breaking every source-reading spec that asserts multi-line \n snippets.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Force LF on everything that a Linux shell/container executes.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
# Git hooks are extensionless POSIX scripts run by git-bash. If they come down as CRLF,
# `exit 1` is neutered — the guard prints "BLOCKED" but the commit still goes through
# (how a fake-secret test fixture once slipped onto main). Force LF so the guards work.
.githooks/** text eol=lf

# COLLABORATE.md is the shared multi-bot coordination thread (append-only).
# union merge: concurrent appends from different bots auto-merge instead of
# conflicting — each bot appends self-contained entries at the end.
COLLABORATE.md merge=union
